## 🤖 FixPilot Autonomous Remediation

### 🎯 Incident / Issue Addressed
> **test**

### 🔍 Root Cause Analysis
Unhandled authentication exception in middleware pipeline

### 🛠️ Applied Solution
Implements token refresh fallback handler with idempotency guard to prevent infinite retry loops. When a 401 authentication error occurs, the middleware checks if a retry has already been attempted. If not, it marks the request with a _retry flag, refreshes the session, and replays the request exactly once. This prevents unhandled authentication exceptions from propagating while avoiding cascading retry failures.

